```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason:  
All three scripts return the same final row, but `1result.sql` accomplishes the task with the clearest, most direct logic—building the required CTEs (`lost_orders`, `order_values`, `category_max`, `avg_val`), then ordering by the distance to the average. It avoids the extra wrapper CTE used in `0result.sql` and the redundant joins/columns found in `2result.sql`, making it the simplest, correct solution.